{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkicbdbsUwTWrodsHiht","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the data layer: cars, parts, tyres, events, licences and all the writing, plus the pure rules for tuning and career."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7450,"cache_read_input_tokens":176969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7450},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c060cbf0-9de2-4b69-aed6-69ef0ff7f0ee","uuid":"f50c2885-4652-424e-af3f-43ce31970a8e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:22:16.559Z","request_id":"req_011CgkicbPinMFyfM6tsq4zx"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkicbdbsUwTWrodsHiht","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WSVd9VgovaTCZLPLeA9e7H","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > src/game/data/meta.js <<'E'\n// Every on-screen use of the title reads this constant.\nexport const TITLE = 'GRANDPA TURISMO';\nexport const SUBTITLE = 'A PATIENT DRIVING LIFE';\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'grandpa-turismo.profile';\nexport const SETTINGS_KEY = 'grandpa-turismo.settings';\nexport const STARTING_CREDITS = 15000;\nexport const PROFILE_VERSION = 3;\nE\ncat > src/game/data/cars.js <<'E'\n// The car table: physics rows (carphysics.js, Appendix B) plus what the menus, sound and models need.\nimport { CARS as PHYS } from './carphysics.js';\nconst row = (id, name, marque, year, price, where, cylinders, exhaust, paint, brochure, shortName, extra = {}) => ({ id, name, marque, year, price, where, cylinders, exhaust, paint, brochure, shortName, phys: PHYS[id], ...extra });\nexport const CAR_LIST = [\n  row('pico', 'TSUBAME PICO 660', 'TSUBAME', 1991, 4800, 'used', 3, { cut: 2600, bite: 0.5, loud: 0.8 }, 'sky', 'A city car of 660 cc, made to fit where other cars can only wish to go. At 720 kg it has little to hold back and little to push. It teaches the first lesson: momentum is expensive.', 'PICO 660'),\n  row('kite', 'TSUBAME KITE 1.6 RS', 'TSUBAME', 1996, 12500, 'used', 4, { cut: 3200, bite: 0.7, loud: 0.9 }, 'red', 'The Kite was a family hatchback until the engineers stayed late. The 1.6-litre engine asks to be revved, and the front tyres do all of the work. Brake before the corner and it will thank you.', 'KITE RS', { fenn: 'A previous owner. One careful weekend. She has 88,000 kilometres and no regrets.' }),\n  row('ginga', 'KAMINARI GINGA S', 'KAMINARI', 1994, 14800, 'used', 6, { cut: 2400, bite: 0.6, loud: 1 }, 'white', 'A front-engined, rear-drive coupe in good used condition. The steering speaks clearly and the rear axle answers the right foot. Many drivers learned to drive in this car. Some learned twice.', 'GINGA S', { fenn: 'One owner. He learned a great deal, and then he bought a sedan.' }),\n  row('moth', 'CASTELLAN MOTH 1.8', 'CASTELLAN', 1998, 24000, 'castellan', 4, { cut: 2800, bite: 0.8, loud: 0.85 }, 'green', 'Two seats, one purpose, 860 kg. Castellan removed what the car did not need, then removed a little more. The power figure is modest. That is not the figure that matters.', 'MOTH 1.8', { fenn: 'I am told the door is optional. I did not ask a second time.' }),\n  row('ryu', 'KAMINARI RYU 2.0T', 'KAMINARI', 1999, 39000, 'kaminari', 4, { cut: 2600, bite: 0.8, loud: 1 }, 'blue', 'Turbocharged, four-wheel drive, born for a rally rule that no longer exists. Power arrives late and then all at once. In the rain, very little can keep it in sight.', 'RYU 2.0T', { fenn: 'Four driven wheels. Please count them. I always do.' }),\n  row('longhorn', 'IRONWOOD LONGHORN 428', 'IRONWOOD', 1969, 47000, 'ironwood', 8, { cut: 1500, bite: 0.9, loud: 1.3 }, 'navy', 'A large American coupe of the old school: seven litres, 420 PS, and brakes that remember a simpler time. It does not like corners, and it says so. On a long straight nobody asks it to apologise.', 'LONGHORN 428', { fenn: 'Seven litres. I had to sit down. Please, take your time.' }),\n  row('brandt32', 'BRANDT 3.2 CSR', 'BRANDT', 2000, 58000, 'brandt', 6, { cut: 3000, bite: 0.6, loud: 1 }, 'slate', 'A four-door sedan, according to the catalogue. The straight six reaches 7,900 rpm with an even temper, and the balance is close to 50:50. Businessmen bought it for the leather. Others did not.', 'BRANDT 3.2', { fenn: 'It has a place for your briefcase. It will not be used.' }),\n  row('heck', 'BRANDT HECK 3.6', 'BRANDT', 1997, 92000, 'brandt', 6, { cut: 2300, bite: 0.9, loud: 1.1 }, 'mist', 'The engine sits behind the rear axle, where Brandt has insisted for forty years that it belongs. Traction is wonderful. Lifting in mid-corner is not recommended. This is written in the manual.', 'HECK 3.6', { fenn: 'Please read page 41 of the manual. Then, please, read it again.' }),\n  row('libeccio', 'VESPUCCI LIBECCIO', 'VESPUCCI', 1995, 135000, 'vespucci', 8, { cut: 3400, bite: 0.8, loud: 1.2 }, 'red', 'Named for the south-west wind. A mid-engined V8 with a low nose and a high opinion of itself. Light on the front wheels at speed. Precise, if you are.', 'LIBECCIO', { fenn: 'One thousand two hundred and fifty kilograms. Excuse me. It is the dust in here.' }),\n  row('kiteCup', 'TSUBAME KITE CUP RACER', 'TSUBAME', 2000, 0, 'prize', 4, { cut: 3800, bite: 1, loud: 1.2 }, 'orange', 'A stripped Kite for a one-make series, with a roll cage where the rear seats used to be. 210 PS through the front wheels asks for a patient foot.', 'KITE CUP'),\n  row('ryuRally', 'KAMINARI RYU RALLY SPEC', 'KAMINARI', 1999, 0, 'prize', 4, { cut: 2800, bite: 1, loud: 1.25 }, 'cyan', 'Works gravel specification: long travel, short gearing, and a bonnet that has seen weather. On dirt it is another species. On tarmac it seems to be looking for the exit.', 'RYU RALLY'),\n  row('works', 'KAMINARI GINGA WORKS GT', 'KAMINARI', 2000, 310000, 'prize', 6, { cut: 4000, bite: 1, loud: 1.4 }, 'plum', 'The Ginga as the factory would like to remember it. 560 PS, carbon panels, and a wing with its own opinion about corner speed.', 'WORKS GT', { afterA: true }),\n  row('corsa', 'VESPUCCI LIBECCIO CORSA', 'VESPUCCI', 1998, 520000, 'prize', 10, { cut: 4600, bite: 1, loud: 1.45 }, 'sand', 'Homologated in the strictest sense of the word: Vespucci built twenty-five road cars so that it could race this one. 620 PS. 1,100 kg. Do not lift.', 'CORSA', { afterA: true }),\n  row('type9', 'HALCYON TYPE 9 PROTOTYPE', 'HALCYON WORKS', 2001, 0, 'prize', 12, { cut: 5200, bite: 1, loud: 1.5 }, 'teal', 'Built by a small works team on the Peninsula, in a shed, for one race. 780 PS, 930 kg, a closed cockpit and no radio. It stops as well as it goes, which takes some time to believe.', 'TYPE 9'),\n];\nexport const CARS = Object.fromEntries(CAR_LIST.map((c) => [c.id, c]));\nexport const SHOWROOMS = [\n  { id: 'used', name: 'USED LOT', line: 'ONE CAREFUL OWNER, OR THEREABOUTS.' },\n  { id: 'kaminari', name: 'KAMINARI', line: 'SERIOUS CARS FOR SERIOUS WEEKENDS.' },\n  { id: 'brandt', name: 'BRANDT', line: 'POLITE AND TERRIFYING SINCE 1948.' },\n  { id: 'imports', name: 'IMPORTS', line: 'CASTELLAN, IRONWOOD AND VESPUCCI. A DIFFICULT FAMILY.' },\n];\n/** Dealer stock: the used lot and three showrooms; the two road-going prize cars join after Licence A. */\nexport function showroomCars(room, licenceA = false) {\n  if (room === 'used') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'used');\n  if (room === 'kaminari') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'kaminari' || (licenceA && c.id === 'works'));\n  if (room === 'brandt') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'brandt');\n  return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => ['castellan', 'ironwood', 'vespucci'].includes(c.where) || (licenceA && c.id === 'corsa'));\n}\nexport const PAINTS = ['red', 'orange', 'sand', 'lime', 'green', 'teal', 'navy', 'blue', 'sky', 'cyan', 'white', 'mist', 'slate', 'night', 'plum', 'ink'];\nexport const RIMS = [\n  { id: 0, name: 'STEEL', hub: 'slate', spoke: 'mist' },\n  { id: 1, name: 'FIVE SPOKE', hub: 'white', spoke: 'mist' },\n  { id: 2, name: 'GOLD MESH', hub: 'sand', spoke: 'orange' },\n  { id: 3, name: 'BLACK RACE', hub: 'ink', spoke: 'red' },\n];\nE\ncat > src/game/data/tyres.js <<'E'\nexport const TYRES = [\n  { id: 'street', name: 'STREET', tyreMu: 0.95, alphaP: 0.14, dirt: 0.45, wearX: 0.8, price: 600, line: 'FOR THE SHOPS. THEY LAST A LONG TIME.' },\n  { id: 'sport', name: 'SPORT', tyreMu: 1.0, alphaP: 0.125, dirt: 0.5, wearX: 1.0, price: 1200, line: 'A GOOD TYRE. THERE IS NOTHING MORE TO SAY.' },\n  { id: 'semi', name: 'SEMI-SLICK', tyreMu: 1.12, alphaP: 0.115, dirt: 0.42, wearX: 1.4, price: 4800, line: 'MORE GRIP. THEY WEAR OUT WHILE YOU WATCH.' },\n  { id: 'slick', name: 'RACING SLICK', tyreMu: 1.3, alphaP: 0.105, dirt: 0.35, wearX: 2.2, price: 12000, line: 'THE MOST GRIP. BRING A SPARE SET AND A STOPWATCH.' },\n  { id: 'rally', name: 'RALLY DIRT', tyreMu: 0.84, alphaP: 0.17, dirt: 0.72, wearX: 1.2, price: 2500, line: 'FOR DIRT. ON TARMAC THEY ARE AN APOLOGY.' },\n];\nexport const TYRE = Object.fromEntries(TYRES.map((t) => [t.id, t]));\nE\ncat > src/game/data/parts.js <<'E'\n// Each part changes numbers in tunedParams (sim/tuning.js). group: parts of one group exclude each other.\n// slots: 'exhaust' etc. live in install.parts as booleans or levels.\nexport const CATEGORIES = [\n  { id: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE', line: 'MORE POWER. IT WILL BE LOUDER AND IT WILL COST MORE.' },\n  { id: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT', line: 'NOTHING IS LIGHTER THAN THE THING YOU REMOVED.' },\n  { id: 'drivetrain', name: 'DRIVETRAIN', line: 'THE ROAD BETWEEN THE ENGINE AND THE TYRE.' },\n  { id: 'suspension', name: 'SUSPENSION', line: 'HOW THE WEIGHT MOVES WHEN YOU ASK IT TO.' },\n  { id: 'brakes', name: 'BRAKES', line: 'THE FASTEST PART OF THE CAR.' },\n  { id: 'aero', name: 'AERO', line: 'AIR IS HEAVY IF YOU GO FAST ENOUGH.' },\n  { id: 'tyres', name: 'TYRES', line: 'FOUR HANDPRINTS OF RUBBER. EVERYTHING ELSE IS OPINION.' },\n  { id: 'body', name: 'BODY', line: 'NO EFFECT ON THE LAP TIME. A LARGE EFFECT ON YOU.' },\n];\nexport const PARTS = [\n  { id: 'exhaust', cat: 'engine', name: 'SPORT EXHAUST', price: 900, line: 'LOUDER, DEEPER. IT CRACKLES WHEN YOU LIFT.', slot: 'exhaust', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'intake', cat: 'engine', name: 'INTAKE AND ECU', price: 1800, line: 'BETTER BREATHING. A SMALL, HONEST GAIN.', slot: 'intake', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'stage1', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 1', price: 3000, line: 'A CAREFUL REBUILD. ABOUT TEN PERCENT.', slot: 'engine', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'stage2', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 2', price: 8000, line: 'HIGHER REVS. ABOUT TWENTY PERCENT.', slot: 'engine', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'stage3', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 3', price: 20000, line: 'NOTHING ORIGINAL REMAINS. ABOUT A THIRD MORE.', slot: 'engine', level: 3 },\n  { id: 'turbo1', cat: 'engine', name: 'TURBO KIT 1', price: 6000, line: 'A SMALL TURBO. IT ARRIVES A LITTLE LATE.', slot: 'turbo', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'turbo2', cat: 'engine', name: 'TURBO KIT 2', price: 15000, line: 'A LARGE TURBO. IT ARRIVES VERY LATE, AND THEN ALL AT ONCE.', slot: 'turbo', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'weight1', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 1', price: 1500, line: 'THE REAR SEATS. YOU WERE NOT USING THEM.', slot: 'weight', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'weight2', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 2', price: 4500, line: 'THE CARPET AND THE RADIO. IT IS QUIETER NOW.', slot: 'weight', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'weight3', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 3', price: 12000, line: 'THIN PANELS AND THIN GLASS. PLEASE CLOSE THE DOOR GENTLY.', slot: 'weight', level: 3 },\n  { id: 'clutch', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'CLUTCH AND FLYWHEEL', price: 1200, line: 'QUICKER GEAR CHANGES.', slot: 'clutch', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'gearbox', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'RACE GEARBOX', price: 5000, line: 'VERY QUICK CHANGES. ADDS A GEARING SETTING.', slot: 'gearbox', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'lsd', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'LIMITED-SLIP DIFF', price: 2500, line: 'BOTH WHEELS PUSH. ADDS AN LSD SETTING.', slot: 'lsd', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'susp1', cat: 'suspension', name: 'SPORT SUSPENSION', price: 2000, line: 'LOWER AND FIRMER. ADDS A BALANCE SETTING.', slot: 'suspension', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'susp2', cat: 'suspension', name: 'RACE SUSPENSION', price: 6000, line: 'ADDS BALANCE AND RIDE HEIGHT. KERBS WILL BE FELT.', slot: 'suspension', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'pads', cat: 'brakes', name: 'SPORT PADS', price: 1500, line: 'THE PEDAL MEANS WHAT IT SAYS.', slot: 'brakes', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'brakekit', cat: 'brakes', name: 'RACE BRAKE KIT', price: 5000, line: 'MUCH LATER BRAKING. ADDS A BRAKE BALANCE SETTING.', slot: 'brakes', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'lip', cat: 'aero', name: 'STREET KIT', price: 2500, line: 'A LIP SPOILER. A LITTLE GRIP, A LITTLE DRAG.', slot: 'aero', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'wing', cat: 'aero', name: 'BIG WING', price: 6000, line: 'MORE DOWNFORCE. MORE DRAG. THERE IS NO THIRD THING.', slot: 'aero', level: 2 },\n];\nexport const PART = Object.fromEntries(PARTS.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\nexport const PAINT_PRICE = 500, RIM_PRICE = 300, OIL_PRICE = 250, WASH_PRICE = 50;\n/** Setup sliders: which part unlocks it, its range, its labels. */\nexport const SETTINGS = [\n  { id: 'gearing', name: 'GEARING', needs: (p) => p.gearbox, min: 0.85, max: 1.15, def: 1, lo: 'TOP SPEED', hi: 'ACCELERATION', line: 'SHORT GEARS PULL HARDER. LONG GEARS GO FURTHER.' },\n  { id: 'lsd', name: 'LSD', needs: (p) => p.lsd, min: 0.2, max: 0.8, def: 0.5, lo: 'FREE', hi: 'LOCKED', line: 'LOCKED PUTS POWER DOWN. FREE TURNS IN.' },\n  { id: 'balance', name: 'BALANCE', needs: (p) => p.suspension, min: 0.45, max: 0.7, def: 0.56, lo: 'TURNS IN', hi: 'STABLE', line: 'THE FRONT OR THE REAR. ONE OF THEM WILL LET GO FIRST.' },\n  { id: 'ride', name: 'RIDE HEIGHT', needs: (p) => p.suspension === 2, min: 0.9, max: 1, def: 1, lo: 'LOW', hi: 'HIGH', line: 'LOW IS QUICK. BELOW A POINT, KERBS JOLT THE BODY.' },\n  { id: 'brakeBias', name: 'BRAKE BALANCE', needs: (p) => p.brakes === 2, min: 0.5, max: 0.75, def: 0.62, lo: 'REAR', hi: 'FRONT', line: 'FRONT IS SAFE. REAR ROTATES THE CAR.' },\n  { id: 'downforce', name: 'DOWNFORCE', needs: (p) => p.aero === 2, min: 0.5, max: 1.5, def: 1, lo: 'LOW', hi: 'HIGH', line: 'CORNERS OR STRAIGHTS. PLEASE CHOOSE.' },\n];\nE\ncat > src/game/sim/tuning.js <<'E'\n// tunedParams(carId, install) → car parameters for the sim, from the stock row plus parts.\nimport { carParams } from './sim.js';\nimport { CARS as PHYS } from '../data/carphysics.js';\nimport { TYRE } from '../data/tyres.js';\nexport const emptyInstall = () => ({ parts: {}, settings: {}, tyre: null, paint: null, rims: 0 });\nconst POWER_ENGINE = [1, 1.10, 1.20, 1.35], RPM_PEAK = [0, 0, 200, 400], RPM_RED = [0, 0, 200, 500];\nexport function tunedRow(carId, install = {}) {\n  const d = { ...PHYS[carId] }, p = install.parts ?? {}, s = install.settings ?? {};\n  let power = 1;\n  if (p.exhaust) power *= 1.04;\n  if (p.intake) power *= 1.06;\n  if (p.engine) { power *= POWER_ENGINE[p.engine]; d.rpmPeak += RPM_PEAK[p.engine]; d.redline += RPM_RED[p.engine]; d.upshift += RPM_RED[p.engine]; }\n  if (p.turbo) {\n    if (d.turbo) power *= p.turbo === 1 ? 1.15 : 1.35;\n    else { power *= p.turbo === 1 ? 1.25 : 1.5; d.turbo = true; d.turboLag = 0.8; }\n  }\n  d.powerPS = Math.round(d.powerPS * power);\n  const cg0 = d.cgH ?? 0.5; let cg = cg0;\n  if (p.weight) { d.massKg = Math.round(d.massKg * [1, 0.95, 0.9, 0.85][p.weight]); cg *= [1, 0.99, 0.98, 0.96][p.weight]; }\n  if (p.clutch) d.shiftTime = 0.11;\n  if (p.gearbox) { d.shiftTime = 0.08; d.final = d.final * (s.gearing ?? 1); }\n  if (p.lsd) d.lsd = s.lsd ?? Math.max(d.lsd ?? 0, 0.5);\n  if (p.suspension === 1) { d.loadK = 0.085; cg *= 0.96; }\n  if (p.suspension === 2) { d.loadK = 0.07; cg *= 0.92; cg *= s.ride ?? 1; }\n  if (p.suspension) d.rollF = s.balance ?? d.rollF;\n  d.cgH = cg;\n  const brakeBase = d.brakeG ?? 1.25;\n  if (p.brakes === 1) d.brakeG = brakeBase + 0.15;\n  if (p.brakes === 2) { d.brakeG = brakeBase + 0.4; d.brakeF = s.brakeBias ?? 0.62; }\n  const clA = d.clA ?? 0.1, cdA = d.cdA ?? 0.7;\n  if (p.aero === 1) { d.clA = clA + 0.15; d.cdA = cdA + 0.02; }\n  if (p.aero === 2) { d.clA = clA + 0.5 * (s.downforce ?? 1); d.cdA = cdA + 0.06 * (s.downforce ?? 1); }\n  if (install.tyre) { const t = TYRE[install.tyre]; d.tyreMu = t.tyreMu; d.alphaP = t.alphaP; d.tyreTable = { dirt: t.dirt, gravel: t.dirt }; d.wearX = t.wearX; }\n  d.exhaustUp = !!p.exhaust;\n  d.jolty = (p.suspension === 2 && (s.ride ?? 1) < 0.94);\n  return d;\n}\nexport const tunedParams = (carId, install) => ({ ...carParams(tunedRow(carId, install)), carId });\n/** Shown power and weight: what event limits read. */\nexport function specOf(carId, install) { const d = tunedRow(carId, install); return { ps: d.powerPS, kg: d.massKg, layout: d.layout, tyre: install?.tyre ?? null }; }\n/** A dyno curve: PS across the rev range, for the before/after draw. */\nexport function dynoCurve(carId, install, torqueShape, points = 40) {\n  const d = tunedRow(carId, install), p = carParams(d), out = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < points; i++) { const rpm = 1500 + ((d.redline - 1500) * i) / (points - 1), x = rpm / d.rpmPeak, boost = d.turbo ? (rpm > d.rpmPeak * 0.4 ? 1 : 0.62) : 1, w = (rpm * 2 * Math.PI) / 60; out.push({ rpm, ps: (p.Tpeak * torqueShape(x, d) * boost * w) / 735.5 }); }\n  return { curve: out, peak: Math.max(...out.map((o) => o.ps)), redline: d.redline };\n}\nE\ncat > src/game/data/licences.js <<'E'\n// Licence tests as data. from/to resolve against a track (corner index c plus metres off, or a raw s from the start line).\nimport { MEDALS } from './medals.gen.js';\nconst t = (id, title, carId, track, o) => ({ id, title, carId, track, medals: MEDALS[id], ...o });\nexport const LICENCES = [\n  { id: 'C', name: 'PROVISIONAL', reward: 2000, goldLine: 'A PICO, AS A PRIZE. PLEASE LOOK AFTER IT.', goldCar: 'pico', blurb: 'THE FIRST CLIPBOARD. THE KITE, THE PROVING GROUND.', tests: ['C-1', 'C-2', 'C-3', 'C-4'] },\n  { id: 'B', name: 'CLUB', reward: 5000, goldLine: 'A CASTELLAN MOTH, AS A PRIZE. IT WAS IN THE WAY.', goldCar: 'moth', blurb: 'REAR-WHEEL DRIVE. KESTREL PARK.', tests: ['B-1', 'B-2', 'B-3', 'B-4'] },\n  { id: 'A', name: 'NATIONAL', reward: 10000, goldLine: '25,000 CREDITS AND A GOLD HELMET FOR THE SHELF.', goldCredits: 25000, goldHelmet: true, blurb: 'CEDAR, RED CLAY AND THE HARBOUR AT NIGHT.', tests: ['A-1', 'A-2', 'A-3', 'A-4'] },\n];\nexport const LICENCE = Object.fromEntries(LICENCES.map((l) => [l.id, l]));\nexport const TESTS = [\n  t('C-1', 'START AND STOP', 'kite', 'proving', { standing: true, from: { s: -300 }, box: { at: 100, len: 30 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'THE BRAKE IS A PEDAL WITH A FAR END.',\n    brief: 'Accelerate to the marker, then bring the car to rest inside the white box. Please remember: the brake is also a steering wheel.', tip: 'BRAKE EARLY. THE BOX WILL WAIT.' }),\n  t('C-2', 'FIRST CORNER', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 0, off: -100 }, to: { c: 1, off: 100 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'TURN IN, APEX, UNWIND.',\n    brief: 'One corner, driven properly. Turn in, touch the apex, and let the car run wide on the way out.', tip: 'SLOW IN, FAST OUT. THIS HAS BEEN TRUE FOR SOME TIME.' }),\n  t('C-3', 'CONE WEAVE', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 50, from: { s: -200 }, to: { s: 200 }, cones: { at: -120, n: 6, gap: 40 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'WEIGHT MOVES.',\n    brief: 'Pass the cones on alternate sides, starting on the left. Each cone hit or missed adds one second. The cones are not angry. They are only cones.', tip: 'STEER EARLY. THE CAR ARRIVES LATER THAN YOU DO.' }),\n  t('C-4', 'THE SHORT LOOP', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 2, off: -50 }, to: { c: 6, off: 50 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'LINK CORNERS. KEEP YOUR HEAD UP.',\n    brief: 'Five corners in a row. Each one begins where the last one ended. Please look ahead of the car.', tip: 'THE EXIT OF ONE CORNER IS THE ENTRY OF THE NEXT.' }),\n  t('B-1', 'THRESHOLD', 'ginga', 'proving', { startSpeed: 160, from: { s: -60 }, box: { at: 105, len: 30 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: { abs: false }, lesson: \"SQUEEZE, DON'T STAMP.\",\n    brief: 'The ABS is off for this test. Stop inside the box. Locking the wheels is allowed. It is not admired.', tip: 'A TYRE THAT IS LOCKED IS ONLY A SLED.' }),\n  t('B-2', 'HAIRPIN EXIT', 'ginga', 'kestrel', { startSpeed: 90, from: { c: 5, off: -150 }, to: { c: 7, off: 60 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: { tcs: 0 }, lesson: 'FEED THE THROTTLE.',\n    brief: 'Traction control is off. The rear tyres will do as they are told, if they are told slowly.', tip: 'OPEN THE THROTTLE AS YOU OPEN THE STEERING.' }),\n  t('B-3', 'THREE LAYOUTS', 'kite', 'proving', { runs: ['kite', 'ginga', 'ryu'], startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'FF, FR, 4WD IN THE SAME CORNERS.',\n    brief: 'The same four corners, in three cars. Front drive, rear drive, all four. The times are added. You will have a favourite. Please keep it to yourself.', tip: 'EACH CAR WANTS A DIFFERENT THROTTLE.' }),\n  t('B-4', 'ONE LAP OF KESTREL', 'ginga', 'kestrel', { flying: true, startSpeed: 110, from: { s: -220 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'RHYTHM.',\n    brief: 'One flying lap of Kestrel Park. The windmill is not part of the course. Many have asked.', tip: 'DO NOT HURRY. BE EARLY.' }),\n  t('A-1', 'BLIND CREST', 'brandt32', 'cedar', { startSpeed: 90, from: { c: 3, off: -100 }, to: { c: 5, off: 100 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'TRUST THE ROAD YOU REMEMBER.',\n    brief: 'The road goes over the crest and turns. You cannot see this. You must remember it.', tip: 'A CREST TAKES WEIGHT FROM ALL FOUR TYRES AT ONCE.' }),\n  t('A-2', 'SWITCHBACKS', 'moth', 'cedar', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'MOMENTUM.',\n    brief: 'The Moth has 135 PS and the road goes uphill. What you have when you arrive is what you keep.', tip: 'A SMOOTH LINE IS A CHEAP SOURCE OF POWER.' }),\n  t('A-3', 'RED CLAY', 'ryuRally', 'redclay', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: false }, assists: {}, lesson: 'ROTATE WITH THE HANDBRAKE.',\n    brief: 'Dirt. Use the handbrake to turn the car in the slow corners. It is not rude here.', tip: 'LOOK WHERE YOU WISH TO GO. THE CAR IS GOING SOMEWHERE ELSE.' }),\n  t('A-4', 'HARBOUR AT NIGHT', 'libeccio', 'harbour', { flying: true, startSpeed: 90, hour: 21, from: { s: -200 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'EVERYTHING, BY LAMPLIGHT.',\n    brief: 'One flying lap of the Harbour. The walls are close and it is dark. There is no margin. I will be here.', tip: 'THE LAMPS MARK THE CORNERS. COUNT THEM.' }),\n];\nexport const TEST = Object.fromEntries(TESTS.map((x) => [x.id, x]));\nE\ncat > src/game/data/medals.gen.js <<'E'\nexport const MEDALS = {};\nE\ncat > src/game/data/events.js <<'E'\n// Events as data. Rounds: [track, laps, {hour, rain}]. pool entries: car id plus an optional tuned install.\nconst T1 = { parts: { exhaust: 1, intake: 1, engine: 1, suspension: 1, weight: 1 }, tyre: 'sport' };\nconst T2 = { parts: { exhaust: 1, intake: 1, engine: 2, suspension: 2, weight: 2, brakes: 1 }, tyre: 'semi' };\nconst r = (track, laps, o = {}) => ({ track, laps, ...o });\nexport const POINTS = [10, 8, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1], PRIZE_RATIO = [1, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2];\nexport const EVENTS = [\n  { id: 'dawn', name: 'DAWN PATROL CUP', needs: 'C', limit: { maxPS: 210 }, limitText: '210 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('kestrel', 2), r('harbour', 2, { hour: 18.5 }), r('kestrel', 3)], pace: [0.86, 0.9], pool: [['pico'], ['kite'], ['moth']], prize: 1500, bonus: 3000,\n    intro: 'A CUP FOR THOSE WHO RISE EARLY AND HAVE NOT YET SPENT MUCH.' },\n  { id: 'fellow', name: 'FRONT-DRIVE FELLOWSHIP', needs: 'C', limit: { maxPS: 230, layout: 'FF' }, limitText: 'FRONT DRIVE, 230 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 2), r('saltline', 4)], pace: [0.88, 0.91], pool: [['kite'], ['kite', T1], ['pico', T1]], prize: 2000, bonus: 5000,\n    intro: 'THE MEMBERS MEET ANNUALLY TO DISCUSS UNDERSTEER. THEY ARE IN FAVOUR.' },\n  { id: 'feather', name: 'FEATHERWEIGHT TROPHY', needs: 'B', limit: { maxKg: 1100 }, limitText: '1,100 KG OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 3), r('kestrel', 3), r('harbour', 3, { hour: 18.5 })], pace: [0.9, 0.93], pool: [['moth'], ['kiteCup'], ['pico', T1]], prize: 3000, bonus: 8000, prizeCar: 'kiteCup',\n    intro: 'THE SCALES ARE CHECKED EACH MORNING. THE DRIVERS HAVE STOPPED EATING LUNCH.' },\n  { id: 'society', name: 'REAR-DRIVE SOCIETY', needs: 'B', limit: { layout: 'FR' }, limitText: 'FRONT ENGINE, REAR DRIVE', rounds: [r('kestrel', 3, { rain: true }), r('saltline', 5)], pace: [0.91, 0.94], pool: [['ginga'], ['brandt32'], ['longhorn']], prize: 3500, bonus: 10000,\n    intro: 'A GENTLE SOCIETY. IT MEETS IN THE RAIN, ON PURPOSE.' },\n  { id: 'clay', name: 'RED CLAY RALLY', needs: 'B', limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR. DIRT TYRES ADVISED', rally: true, rounds: [r('redclay', 2), r('redclay', 2), r('redclay', 2)], pace: [0.91, 0.95], pool: [['ryu'], ['ryuRally']], prize: 4000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'ryuRally',\n    intro: 'THREE LEGS AGAINST ONE RIVAL EACH. WIN TWO. THE CLOCK DECIDES.' },\n  { id: 'touring', name: 'PENINSULA TOURING TROPHY', needs: 'A', limit: { maxPS: 520 }, limitText: '520 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 3), r('harbour', 3, { hour: 21 }), r('saltline', 6), r('kestrel', 4)], pace: [0.93, 0.96], pool: [['brandt32'], ['heck'], ['libeccio'], ['longhorn'], ['ryu', T1]], prize: 6000, bonus: 40000, prizeCar: 'corsa',\n    intro: 'FOUR ROUNDS, THE WHOLE PENINSULA. BRING A SANDWICH.' },\n  { id: 'h200', name: 'HARBOUR LIGHTS 200', needs: 'A', limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR. ONE PIT STOP NEEDED', endurance: true, rounds: [r('harbour', 10, { hour: 18.5, hourEnd: 21 })], pace: [0.92, 0.95], pool: [['heck'], ['libeccio'], ['brandt32', T2]], prize: 20000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'works', field: 8,\n    intro: 'TEN LAPS, DUSK INTO NIGHT. THE TYRES WILL NOT LAST. THE FUEL WILL NOT LAST. PLEASE STOP ONCE.' },\n  { id: 'gp', name: 'THE HALCYON GRAND PRIX', needs: 'A', needsEvent: ['touring', 'h200'], limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR', rounds: [r('kestrel', 5), r('cedar', 5), r('saltline', 8), r('harbour', 5, { hour: 21 })], pace: [0.96, 0.99], pool: [['works'], ['corsa'], ['libeccio', T2]], prize: 30000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'type9', ending: true,\n    intro: 'THE LAST EVENT. THE PENINSULA WILL BE WATCHING, IN ITS QUIET WAY.' },\n];\nexport const EVENT = Object.fromEntries(EVENTS.map((e) => [e.id, e]));\nexport const DRIVERS = ['A. MORETTI', 'K. HANDA', 'J. OAKES', 'L. BRANDVOLD', 'S. AOKI', 'P. DELACROIX', 'T. WREN', 'R. OSEI', 'M. VANTER', 'D. IGARASHI', 'C. HOLLOWAY', 'E. RASK'];\nE\ncat > src/game/sim/career.js <<'E'\n// Pure rules of the career: money, licences, events, prizes, oil, days. No engine, no DOM.\nimport { CARS, CAR_LIST } from '../data/cars.js';\nimport { PART, PAINT_PRICE, RIM_PRICE, OIL_PRICE, WASH_PRICE, SETTINGS } from '../data/parts.js';\nimport { TYRE } from '../data/tyres.js';\nimport { LICENCES, LICENCE, TEST } from '../data/licences.js';\nimport { EVENT, EVENTS, POINTS, PRIZE_RATIO } from '../data/events.js';\nimport { STARTING_CREDITS, PROFILE_VERSION } from '../data/meta.js';\nimport { specOf, emptyInstall } from './tuning.js';\n\nexport function newProfile() {\n  return { v: PROFILE_VERSION, credits: STARTING_CREDITS, day: 1, cars: [], current: null, nextUid: 1, tests: {}, licences: {}, events: {}, seen: {}, trophies: [], assists: { abs: true, tcs: 5, asm: 5, auto: true, line: false }, records: {}, stats: { km: 0, wins: 0, races: 0, golds: 0, spent: 0, earned: 0 }, greeted: false, ended: false, replays: [], ghosts: {}, failStreak: {} };\n}\n/** Older saves move forward one version at a time. */\nexport function migrate(p) {\n  if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return newProfile();\n  if (!p.v || p.v < 2) { p.seen ??= {}; p.trophies ??= []; p.v = 2; }\n  if (p.v < 3) { p.replays ??= []; p.ghosts ??= {}; p.failStreak ??= {}; for (const c of p.cars ?? []) { c.dirt ??= 0; c.oilKm ??= 0; c.install ??= emptyInstall(); } p.v = 3; }\n  return p;\n}\nexport const carRec = (p, uid = p.current) => p.cars.find((c) => c.uid === uid) ?? null;\nexport const hasCar = (p, id) => p.cars.some((c) => c.id === id);\nfunction giveCar(p, id, bought) {\n  const rec = { uid: p.nextUid++, id, install: emptyInstall(), km: bought ? 40000 + (id.length * 7919) % 50000 : 0, oilKm: bought && CARS[id].where === 'used' ? 900 : 0, dirt: 0, wins: 0, prize: !bought };\n  if (CARS[id].where !== 'used') rec.km = bought ? 12 : 0;\n  rec.install.paint = CARS[id].paint;\n  p.cars.push(rec); p.seen[id] = true;\n  if (p.current == null) p.current = rec.uid;\n  return rec;\n}\nexport function canBuy(p, id) {\n  const c = CARS[id];\n  if (!c.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT FOR SALE' };\n  if (c.afterA && !p.licences.A) return { ok: false, why: 'LICENCE A REQUIRED' };\n  if (p.credits < c.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT ENOUGH CREDITS' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function buyCar(p, id) { const can = canBuy(p, id); if (!can.ok) return null; p.credits -= CARS[id].price; p.stats.spent += CARS[id].price; const rec = giveCar(p, id, true); p.current = rec.uid; return rec; }\nexport function canSell(p, uid) {\n  const r = carRec(p, uid);\n  if (!r) return { ok: false, why: 'NO SUCH CAR' };\n  if (p.cars.length <= 1) return { ok: false, why: 'YOUR LAST CAR. THEN WHAT?' };\n  if (r.prize) return { ok: false, why: 'PRIZE CARS ARE NOT FOR SALE. IT IS SIMPLY NOT DONE.' };\n  return { ok: true, value: Math.floor(CARS[r.id].price / 2) };\n}\nexport function sellCar(p, uid) { const can = canSell(p, uid); if (!can.ok) return 0; p.credits += can.value; p.cars = p.cars.filter((c) => c.uid !== uid); if (p.current === uid) p.current = p.cars[0].uid; return can.value; }\n\n// ---- parts\nexport function partOwned(rec, part) { const v = rec.install.parts[part.slot]; return part.level === v; }\nexport function partSuperseded(rec, part) { const v = rec.install.parts[part.slot]; return !!v && v > part.level; }\nexport function canBuyPart(p, rec, part) {\n  if (partOwned(rec, part)) return { ok: false, why: 'FITTED' };\n  if (p.credits < part.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT ENOUGH CREDITS' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function buyPart(p, rec, partId) {\n  const part = PART[partId], can = canBuyPart(p, rec, part);\n  if (!can.ok) return false;\n  p.credits -= part.price; p.stats.spent += part.price; rec.install.parts[part.slot] = part.level;\n  for (const s of SETTINGS) if (s.needs(rec.install.parts) && rec.install.settings[s.id] == null) rec.install.settings[s.id] = s.id === 'balance' ? CARS[rec.id].phys.rollF ?? s.def : s.def;\n  return true;\n}\nexport function buyTyre(p, rec, id) { const t = TYRE[id]; if (rec.install.tyre === id || p.credits < t.price) return false; p.credits -= t.price; p.stats.spent += t.price; rec.install.tyre = id; return true; }\nexport function buyPaint(p, rec, colour) { if (p.credits < PAINT_PRICE || rec.install.paint === colour) return false; p.credits -= PAINT_PRICE; p.stats.spent += PAINT_PRICE; rec.install.paint = colour; return true; }\nexport function buyRims(p, rec, id) { if (p.credits < RIM_PRICE || rec.install.rims === id) return false; p.credits -= RIM_PRICE; p.stats.spent += RIM_PRICE; rec.install.rims = id; return true; }\n\n// ---- service\nexport function oilFactor(rec) {\n  const km = rec?.oilKm ?? 0;\n  if (km < 100 && rec?.oilFresh) return 1.02;\n  if (km <= 200) return 1;\n  return Math.max(0.92, 1 - Math.floor((km - 200) / 40) * 0.005);\n}\nexport function changeOil(p, rec) { if (p.credits < OIL_PRICE) return false; p.credits -= OIL_PRICE; p.stats.spent += OIL_PRICE; rec.oilKm = 0; rec.oilFresh = true; return true; }\nexport function washCar(p, rec) { if (p.credits < WASH_PRICE) return false; p.credits -= WASH_PRICE; p.stats.spent += WASH_PRICE; rec.dirt = 0; return true; }\nexport function addMileage(p, rec, metres, dirtGain = 0) { const km = metres / 1000; p.stats.km += km; if (rec) { rec.km += km; rec.oilKm += km; rec.dirt = Math.min(1, rec.dirt + dirtGain); } }\n\n// ---- licences\nexport const licenceOrder = ['C', 'B', 'A'];\nexport const licenceHeld = (p, id) => !!p.licences[id];\nexport const licenceOpen = (p, id) => id === 'C' || licenceHeld(p, licenceOrder[licenceOrder.indexOf(id) - 1]);\nexport const medalName = (m) => [null, 'BRONZE', 'SILVER', 'GOLD'][m];\nexport function medalFor(test, time) { const m = test.medals; if (!m) return 0; return time <= m.gold ? 3 : time <= m.silver ? 2 : time <= m.bronze ? 1 : 0; }\n/** Record an attempt; returns what happened so the screens can say it. */\nexport function applyTest(p, testId, time, failed = false, dev = false) {\n  const test = TEST[testId], medal = failed ? 0 : medalFor(test, time), out = { medal, licenceWon: null, reward: 0, goldBonus: null, newBest: false };\n  if (medal === 0) { p.failStreak[testId] = (p.failStreak[testId] ?? 0) + 1; return out; }\n  p.failStreak[testId] = 0;\n  if (dev) return out;\n  const prev = p.tests[testId] ?? { medal: 0, time: Infinity };\n  if (medal === 3 && prev.medal < 3) p.stats.golds++;\n  if (medal > prev.medal || time < prev.time) out.newBest = true;\n  p.tests[testId] = { medal: Math.max(prev.medal, medal), time: Math.min(prev.time, time) };\n  const lic = LICENCE[testId[0]];\n  if (!p.licences[lic.id] && lic.tests.every((t) => p.tests[t]?.medal >= 1)) { p.licences[lic.id] = true; p.credits += lic.reward; p.stats.earned += lic.reward; out.licenceWon = lic.id; out.reward = lic.reward; }\n  if (p.licences[lic.id] && !p.goldDone?.[lic.id] && lic.tests.every((t) => p.tests[t]?.medal === 3)) {\n    (p.goldDone ??= {})[lic.id] = true; out.goldBonus = lic.id;\n    if (lic.goldCar && !hasCar(p, lic.goldCar)) giveCar(p, lic.goldCar, false);\n    if (lic.goldCredits) { p.credits += lic.goldCredits; p.stats.earned += lic.goldCredits; }\n    if (lic.goldHelmet) p.trophies.push({ kind: 'helmet', name: `GOLD HELMET`, day: p.day });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n// ---- events\nexport function eventOpen(p, id) {\n  const e = EVENT[id];\n  if (!p.licences[e.needs]) return { ok: false, why: `LICENCE ${e.needs} REQUIRED` };\n  if (e.needsEvent && !e.needsEvent.some((x) => p.events[x]?.won)) return { ok: false, why: 'WIN THE TOURING TROPHY OR THE HARBOUR 200' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function carQualifies(e, carId, install) {\n  const s = specOf(carId, install), l = e.limit;\n  if (l.maxPS && s.ps > l.maxPS) return { ok: false, why: `${s.ps} PS. THE LIMIT IS ${l.maxPS}.` };\n  if (l.maxKg && s.kg > l.maxKg) return { ok: false, why: `${s.kg} KG. THE LIMIT IS ${l.maxKg}.` };\n  if (l.layout && s.layout !== l.layout) return { ok: false, why: `THIS EVENT IS FOR ${l.layout} CARS ONLY.` };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport const eventState = (p, id) => (p.events[id] ??= { round: 0, points: {}, won: false, wins: 0, best: null });\n/** results: [{ key, name, player }] in finishing order. Returns the money and the state of the series. */\nexport function applyRound(p, eventId, results, prizeScale = 1) {\n  const e = EVENT[eventId], st = eventState(p, eventId), out = { place: 0, money: 0, points: 0, seriesOver: false, seriesWon: false, bonus: 0, prizeCar: null, standings: [], ending: false };\n  results.forEach((r, i) => { const pts = POINTS[i] ?? 0; st.points[r.key] = (st.points[r.key] ?? 0) + pts; if (r.player) { out.place = i + 1; out.points = pts; } });\n  out.money = Math.round(((PRIZE_RATIO[out.place - 1] ?? 0) * e.prize * prizeScale) / 10) * 10;\n  p.credits += out.money; p.stats.earned += out.money; p.stats.races++; p.day++;\n  if (out.place === 1) p.stats.wins++;\n  st.round++;\n  out.standings = Object.entries(st.points).sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);\n  if (st.round >= e.rounds.length) {\n    out.seriesOver = true;\n    const my = st.points.player ?? 0, top = Math.max(...Object.entries(st.points).filter(([k]) => k !== 'player').map(([, v]) => v), 0);\n    out.seriesWon = my > top;\n    if (out.seriesWon) {\n      const first = !st.won;\n      st.won = true; st.wins = (st.wins ?? 0) + 1; out.bonus = Math.round(e.bonus * prizeScale); p.credits += out.bonus; p.stats.earned += out.bonus;\n      if (e.prizeCar && first && !hasCar(p, e.prizeCar)) { giveCar(p, e.prizeCar, false); out.prizeCar = e.prizeCar; }\n      p.trophies.push({ kind: 'cup', name: e.name, day: p.day });\n      if (e.ending && first) { out.ending = true; p.ended = true; }\n    }\n    st.round = 0; st.points = {};\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nexport function resetEvent(p, id) { const st = eventState(p, id); st.round = 0; st.points = {}; }\n\nexport function record(p, trackId, lap, carName) { const r = p.records[trackId]; if (!r || lap < r.lap) { p.records[trackId] = { lap, car: carName }; return true; } return false; }\n/** Share of the world collected, for the Garage. */\nexport function collected(p) {\n  const cars = new Set(p.cars.map((c) => c.id)).size, tests = Object.keys(p.tests).length, ev = EVENTS.filter((e) => p.events[e.id]?.won).length;\n  return Math.round(((cars + tests + ev) / (CAR_LIST.length + 12 + EVENTS.length)) * 100);\n}\n/** One line saying what to try next on the Map. */\nexport function nudge(p) {\n  if (!p.cars.length) return { place: 'dealer', text: 'FIRST, A CAR. DEALER ROW HAS THREE YOU CAN AFFORD.' };\n  if (!p.licences.C) return { place: 'licence', text: 'NOW, A LICENCE. MS. ARAI IS WAITING AT THE TOWER.' };\n  if (!EVENT.dawn || !p.events.dawn?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE DAWN PATROL CUP WILL ACCEPT YOU. THE EVENT HALL IS OPEN.' };\n  const r = carRec(p);\n  if (r && r.oilKm > 300) return { place: 'service', text: 'YOUR OIL IS TIRED. BENNO HAS MENTIONED IT.' };\n  if (!Object.keys(r?.install.parts ?? {}).length) return { place: 'tuning', text: 'YOU HAVE MONEY. BRAKE PADS ARE A GOOD FIRST THOUGHT.' };\n  if (!p.licences.B) return { place: 'licence', text: 'THE CLUB LICENCE IS NEXT. PLEASE BRING A REAR-DRIVE ATTITUDE.' };\n  if (!p.events.feather?.won && !p.events.society?.won && !p.events.clay?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THREE NEW EVENTS AWAIT THE CLUB LICENCE.' };\n  if (!p.licences.A) return { place: 'licence', text: 'THE NATIONAL LICENCE. MS. ARAI HAS CLEARED HER AFTERNOON.' };\n  if (!p.events.touring?.won && !p.events.h200?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE TOURING TROPHY AND THE HARBOUR 200 ARE OPEN TO YOU.' };\n  if (!p.events.gp?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE GRAND PRIX. THE LIGHTS ARE ON FOR YOU NOW.' };\n  return { place: 'home', text: 'YOU MAY KEEP DRIVING. MOST PEOPLE DO.' };\n}\nexport { LICENCES, EVENTS };\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\nprint(\"ok\")\nE\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'E'\n- Sim extracted from plan and passes lap regression (tools/tests/reg0.mjs -> move into sim suite). data/* and sim/career, tuning written.\nE\nls ..","description":"Write data modules, tuning and career rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7450,"cache_read_input_tokens":176969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7450},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c060cbf0-9de2-4b69-aed6-69ef0ff7f0ee","uuid":"9ccbbd3a-f727-43f8-8270-2f195d4f8b90","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:24:45.491Z","request_id":"req_011CgkicbPinMFyfM6tsq4zx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WSVd9VgovaTCZLPLeA9e7H":{"command":"cat > src/game/data/meta.js <<'E'\n// Every on-screen use of the title reads this constant.\nexport const TITLE = 'GRANDPA TURISMO';\nexport const SUBTITLE = 'A PATIENT DRIVING LIFE';\nexport const SAVE_KEY = 'grandpa-turismo.profile';\nexport const SETTINGS_KEY = 'grandpa-turismo.settings';\nexport const STARTING_CREDITS = 15000;\nexport const PROFILE_VERSION = 3;\nE\ncat > src/game/data/cars.js <<'E'\n// The car table: physics rows (carphysics.js, Appendix B) plus what the menus, sound and models need.\nimport { CARS as PHYS } from './carphysics.js';\nconst row = (id, name, marque, year, price, where, cylinders, exhaust, paint, brochure, shortName, extra = {}) => ({ id, name, marque, year, price, where, cylinders, exhaust, paint, brochure, shortName, phys: PHYS[id], ...extra });\nexport const CAR_LIST = [\n  row('pico', 'TSUBAME PICO 660', 'TSUBAME', 1991, 4800, 'used', 3, { cut: 2600, bite: 0.5, loud: 0.8 }, 'sky', 'A city car of 660 cc, made to fit where other cars can only wish to go. At 720 kg it has little to hold back and little to push. It teaches the first lesson: momentum is expensive.', 'PICO 660'),\n  row('kite', 'TSUBAME KITE 1.6 RS', 'TSUBAME', 1996, 12500, 'used', 4, { cut: 3200, bite: 0.7, loud: 0.9 }, 'red', 'The Kite was a family hatchback until the engineers stayed late. The 1.6-litre engine asks to be revved, and the front tyres do all of the work. Brake before the corner and it will thank you.', 'KITE RS', { fenn: 'A previous owner. One careful weekend. She has 88,000 kilometres and no regrets.' }),\n  row('ginga', 'KAMINARI GINGA S', 'KAMINARI', 1994, 14800, 'used', 6, { cut: 2400, bite: 0.6, loud: 1 }, 'white', 'A front-engined, rear-drive coupe in good used condition. The steering speaks clearly and the rear axle answers the right foot. Many drivers learned to drive in this car. Some learned twice.', 'GINGA S', { fenn: 'One owner. He learned a great deal, and then he bought a sedan.' }),\n  row('moth', 'CASTELLAN MOTH 1.8', 'CASTELLAN', 1998, 24000, 'castellan', 4, { cut: 2800, bite: 0.8, loud: 0.85 }, 'green', 'Two seats, one purpose, 860 kg. Castellan removed what the car did not need, then removed a little more. The power figure is modest. That is not the figure that matters.', 'MOTH 1.8', { fenn: 'I am told the door is optional. I did not ask a second time.' }),\n  row('ryu', 'KAMINARI RYU 2.0T', 'KAMINARI', 1999, 39000, 'kaminari', 4, { cut: 2600, bite: 0.8, loud: 1 }, 'blue', 'Turbocharged, four-wheel drive, born for a rally rule that no longer exists. Power arrives late and then all at once. In the rain, very little can keep it in sight.', 'RYU 2.0T', { fenn: 'Four driven wheels. Please count them. I always do.' }),\n  row('longhorn', 'IRONWOOD LONGHORN 428', 'IRONWOOD', 1969, 47000, 'ironwood', 8, { cut: 1500, bite: 0.9, loud: 1.3 }, 'navy', 'A large American coupe of the old school: seven litres, 420 PS, and brakes that remember a simpler time. It does not like corners, and it says so. On a long straight nobody asks it to apologise.', 'LONGHORN 428', { fenn: 'Seven litres. I had to sit down. Please, take your time.' }),\n  row('brandt32', 'BRANDT 3.2 CSR', 'BRANDT', 2000, 58000, 'brandt', 6, { cut: 3000, bite: 0.6, loud: 1 }, 'slate', 'A four-door sedan, according to the catalogue. The straight six reaches 7,900 rpm with an even temper, and the balance is close to 50:50. Businessmen bought it for the leather. Others did not.', 'BRANDT 3.2', { fenn: 'It has a place for your briefcase. It will not be used.' }),\n  row('heck', 'BRANDT HECK 3.6', 'BRANDT', 1997, 92000, 'brandt', 6, { cut: 2300, bite: 0.9, loud: 1.1 }, 'mist', 'The engine sits behind the rear axle, where Brandt has insisted for forty years that it belongs. Traction is wonderful. Lifting in mid-corner is not recommended. This is written in the manual.', 'HECK 3.6', { fenn: 'Please read page 41 of the manual. Then, please, read it again.' }),\n  row('libeccio', 'VESPUCCI LIBECCIO', 'VESPUCCI', 1995, 135000, 'vespucci', 8, { cut: 3400, bite: 0.8, loud: 1.2 }, 'red', 'Named for the south-west wind. A mid-engined V8 with a low nose and a high opinion of itself. Light on the front wheels at speed. Precise, if you are.', 'LIBECCIO', { fenn: 'One thousand two hundred and fifty kilograms. Excuse me. It is the dust in here.' }),\n  row('kiteCup', 'TSUBAME KITE CUP RACER', 'TSUBAME', 2000, 0, 'prize', 4, { cut: 3800, bite: 1, loud: 1.2 }, 'orange', 'A stripped Kite for a one-make series, with a roll cage where the rear seats used to be. 210 PS through the front wheels asks for a patient foot.', 'KITE CUP'),\n  row('ryuRally', 'KAMINARI RYU RALLY SPEC', 'KAMINARI', 1999, 0, 'prize', 4, { cut: 2800, bite: 1, loud: 1.25 }, 'cyan', 'Works gravel specification: long travel, short gearing, and a bonnet that has seen weather. On dirt it is another species. On tarmac it seems to be looking for the exit.', 'RYU RALLY'),\n  row('works', 'KAMINARI GINGA WORKS GT', 'KAMINARI', 2000, 310000, 'prize', 6, { cut: 4000, bite: 1, loud: 1.4 }, 'plum', 'The Ginga as the factory would like to remember it. 560 PS, carbon panels, and a wing with its own opinion about corner speed.', 'WORKS GT', { afterA: true }),\n  row('corsa', 'VESPUCCI LIBECCIO CORSA', 'VESPUCCI', 1998, 520000, 'prize', 10, { cut: 4600, bite: 1, loud: 1.45 }, 'sand', 'Homologated in the strictest sense of the word: Vespucci built twenty-five road cars so that it could race this one. 620 PS. 1,100 kg. Do not lift.', 'CORSA', { afterA: true }),\n  row('type9', 'HALCYON TYPE 9 PROTOTYPE', 'HALCYON WORKS', 2001, 0, 'prize', 12, { cut: 5200, bite: 1, loud: 1.5 }, 'teal', 'Built by a small works team on the Peninsula, in a shed, for one race. 780 PS, 930 kg, a closed cockpit and no radio. It stops as well as it goes, which takes some time to believe.', 'TYPE 9'),\n];\nexport const CARS = Object.fromEntries(CAR_LIST.map((c) => [c.id, c]));\nexport const SHOWROOMS = [\n  { id: 'used', name: 'USED LOT', line: 'ONE CAREFUL OWNER, OR THEREABOUTS.' },\n  { id: 'kaminari', name: 'KAMINARI', line: 'SERIOUS CARS FOR SERIOUS WEEKENDS.' },\n  { id: 'brandt', name: 'BRANDT', line: 'POLITE AND TERRIFYING SINCE 1948.' },\n  { id: 'imports', name: 'IMPORTS', line: 'CASTELLAN, IRONWOOD AND VESPUCCI. A DIFFICULT FAMILY.' },\n];\n/** Dealer stock: the used lot and three showrooms; the two road-going prize cars join after Licence A. */\nexport function showroomCars(room, licenceA = false) {\n  if (room === 'used') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'used');\n  if (room === 'kaminari') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'kaminari' || (licenceA && c.id === 'works'));\n  if (room === 'brandt') return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => c.where === 'brandt');\n  return CAR_LIST.filter((c) => ['castellan', 'ironwood', 'vespucci'].includes(c.where) || (licenceA && c.id === 'corsa'));\n}\nexport const PAINTS = ['red', 'orange', 'sand', 'lime', 'green', 'teal', 'navy', 'blue', 'sky', 'cyan', 'white', 'mist', 'slate', 'night', 'plum', 'ink'];\nexport const RIMS = [\n  { id: 0, name: 'STEEL', hub: 'slate', spoke: 'mist' },\n  { id: 1, name: 'FIVE SPOKE', hub: 'white', spoke: 'mist' },\n  { id: 2, name: 'GOLD MESH', hub: 'sand', spoke: 'orange' },\n  { id: 3, name: 'BLACK RACE', hub: 'ink', spoke: 'red' },\n];\nE\ncat > src/game/data/tyres.js <<'E'\nexport const TYRES = [\n  { id: 'street', name: 'STREET', tyreMu: 0.95, alphaP: 0.14, dirt: 0.45, wearX: 0.8, price: 600, line: 'FOR THE SHOPS. THEY LAST A LONG TIME.' },\n  { id: 'sport', name: 'SPORT', tyreMu: 1.0, alphaP: 0.125, dirt: 0.5, wearX: 1.0, price: 1200, line: 'A GOOD TYRE. THERE IS NOTHING MORE TO SAY.' },\n  { id: 'semi', name: 'SEMI-SLICK', tyreMu: 1.12, alphaP: 0.115, dirt: 0.42, wearX: 1.4, price: 4800, line: 'MORE GRIP. THEY WEAR OUT WHILE YOU WATCH.' },\n  { id: 'slick', name: 'RACING SLICK', tyreMu: 1.3, alphaP: 0.105, dirt: 0.35, wearX: 2.2, price: 12000, line: 'THE MOST GRIP. BRING A SPARE SET AND A STOPWATCH.' },\n  { id: 'rally', name: 'RALLY DIRT', tyreMu: 0.84, alphaP: 0.17, dirt: 0.72, wearX: 1.2, price: 2500, line: 'FOR DIRT. ON TARMAC THEY ARE AN APOLOGY.' },\n];\nexport const TYRE = Object.fromEntries(TYRES.map((t) => [t.id, t]));\nE\ncat > src/game/data/parts.js <<'E'\n// Each part changes numbers in tunedParams (sim/tuning.js). group: parts of one group exclude each other.\n// slots: 'exhaust' etc. live in install.parts as booleans or levels.\nexport const CATEGORIES = [\n  { id: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE', line: 'MORE POWER. IT WILL BE LOUDER AND IT WILL COST MORE.' },\n  { id: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT', line: 'NOTHING IS LIGHTER THAN THE THING YOU REMOVED.' },\n  { id: 'drivetrain', name: 'DRIVETRAIN', line: 'THE ROAD BETWEEN THE ENGINE AND THE TYRE.' },\n  { id: 'suspension', name: 'SUSPENSION', line: 'HOW THE WEIGHT MOVES WHEN YOU ASK IT TO.' },\n  { id: 'brakes', name: 'BRAKES', line: 'THE FASTEST PART OF THE CAR.' },\n  { id: 'aero', name: 'AERO', line: 'AIR IS HEAVY IF YOU GO FAST ENOUGH.' },\n  { id: 'tyres', name: 'TYRES', line: 'FOUR HANDPRINTS OF RUBBER. EVERYTHING ELSE IS OPINION.' },\n  { id: 'body', name: 'BODY', line: 'NO EFFECT ON THE LAP TIME. A LARGE EFFECT ON YOU.' },\n];\nexport const PARTS = [\n  { id: 'exhaust', cat: 'engine', name: 'SPORT EXHAUST', price: 900, line: 'LOUDER, DEEPER. IT CRACKLES WHEN YOU LIFT.', slot: 'exhaust', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'intake', cat: 'engine', name: 'INTAKE AND ECU', price: 1800, line: 'BETTER BREATHING. A SMALL, HONEST GAIN.', slot: 'intake', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'stage1', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 1', price: 3000, line: 'A CAREFUL REBUILD. ABOUT TEN PERCENT.', slot: 'engine', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'stage2', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 2', price: 8000, line: 'HIGHER REVS. ABOUT TWENTY PERCENT.', slot: 'engine', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'stage3', cat: 'engine', name: 'ENGINE STAGE 3', price: 20000, line: 'NOTHING ORIGINAL REMAINS. ABOUT A THIRD MORE.', slot: 'engine', level: 3 },\n  { id: 'turbo1', cat: 'engine', name: 'TURBO KIT 1', price: 6000, line: 'A SMALL TURBO. IT ARRIVES A LITTLE LATE.', slot: 'turbo', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'turbo2', cat: 'engine', name: 'TURBO KIT 2', price: 15000, line: 'A LARGE TURBO. IT ARRIVES VERY LATE, AND THEN ALL AT ONCE.', slot: 'turbo', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'weight1', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 1', price: 1500, line: 'THE REAR SEATS. YOU WERE NOT USING THEM.', slot: 'weight', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'weight2', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 2', price: 4500, line: 'THE CARPET AND THE RADIO. IT IS QUIETER NOW.', slot: 'weight', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'weight3', cat: 'weight', name: 'WEIGHT STAGE 3', price: 12000, line: 'THIN PANELS AND THIN GLASS. PLEASE CLOSE THE DOOR GENTLY.', slot: 'weight', level: 3 },\n  { id: 'clutch', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'CLUTCH AND FLYWHEEL', price: 1200, line: 'QUICKER GEAR CHANGES.', slot: 'clutch', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'gearbox', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'RACE GEARBOX', price: 5000, line: 'VERY QUICK CHANGES. ADDS A GEARING SETTING.', slot: 'gearbox', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'lsd', cat: 'drivetrain', name: 'LIMITED-SLIP DIFF', price: 2500, line: 'BOTH WHEELS PUSH. ADDS AN LSD SETTING.', slot: 'lsd', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'susp1', cat: 'suspension', name: 'SPORT SUSPENSION', price: 2000, line: 'LOWER AND FIRMER. ADDS A BALANCE SETTING.', slot: 'suspension', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'susp2', cat: 'suspension', name: 'RACE SUSPENSION', price: 6000, line: 'ADDS BALANCE AND RIDE HEIGHT. KERBS WILL BE FELT.', slot: 'suspension', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'pads', cat: 'brakes', name: 'SPORT PADS', price: 1500, line: 'THE PEDAL MEANS WHAT IT SAYS.', slot: 'brakes', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'brakekit', cat: 'brakes', name: 'RACE BRAKE KIT', price: 5000, line: 'MUCH LATER BRAKING. ADDS A BRAKE BALANCE SETTING.', slot: 'brakes', level: 2 },\n  { id: 'lip', cat: 'aero', name: 'STREET KIT', price: 2500, line: 'A LIP SPOILER. A LITTLE GRIP, A LITTLE DRAG.', slot: 'aero', level: 1 },\n  { id: 'wing', cat: 'aero', name: 'BIG WING', price: 6000, line: 'MORE DOWNFORCE. MORE DRAG. THERE IS NO THIRD THING.', slot: 'aero', level: 2 },\n];\nexport const PART = Object.fromEntries(PARTS.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\nexport const PAINT_PRICE = 500, RIM_PRICE = 300, OIL_PRICE = 250, WASH_PRICE = 50;\n/** Setup sliders: which part unlocks it, its range, its labels. */\nexport const SETTINGS = [\n  { id: 'gearing', name: 'GEARING', needs: (p) => p.gearbox, min: 0.85, max: 1.15, def: 1, lo: 'TOP SPEED', hi: 'ACCELERATION', line: 'SHORT GEARS PULL HARDER. LONG GEARS GO FURTHER.' },\n  { id: 'lsd', name: 'LSD', needs: (p) => p.lsd, min: 0.2, max: 0.8, def: 0.5, lo: 'FREE', hi: 'LOCKED', line: 'LOCKED PUTS POWER DOWN. FREE TURNS IN.' },\n  { id: 'balance', name: 'BALANCE', needs: (p) => p.suspension, min: 0.45, max: 0.7, def: 0.56, lo: 'TURNS IN', hi: 'STABLE', line: 'THE FRONT OR THE REAR. ONE OF THEM WILL LET GO FIRST.' },\n  { id: 'ride', name: 'RIDE HEIGHT', needs: (p) => p.suspension === 2, min: 0.9, max: 1, def: 1, lo: 'LOW', hi: 'HIGH', line: 'LOW IS QUICK. BELOW A POINT, KERBS JOLT THE BODY.' },\n  { id: 'brakeBias', name: 'BRAKE BALANCE', needs: (p) => p.brakes === 2, min: 0.5, max: 0.75, def: 0.62, lo: 'REAR', hi: 'FRONT', line: 'FRONT IS SAFE. REAR ROTATES THE CAR.' },\n  { id: 'downforce', name: 'DOWNFORCE', needs: (p) => p.aero === 2, min: 0.5, max: 1.5, def: 1, lo: 'LOW', hi: 'HIGH', line: 'CORNERS OR STRAIGHTS. PLEASE CHOOSE.' },\n];\nE\ncat > src/game/sim/tuning.js <<'E'\n// tunedParams(carId, install) → car parameters for the sim, from the stock row plus parts.\nimport { carParams } from './sim.js';\nimport { CARS as PHYS } from '../data/carphysics.js';\nimport { TYRE } from '../data/tyres.js';\nexport const emptyInstall = () => ({ parts: {}, settings: {}, tyre: null, paint: null, rims: 0 });\nconst POWER_ENGINE = [1, 1.10, 1.20, 1.35], RPM_PEAK = [0, 0, 200, 400], RPM_RED = [0, 0, 200, 500];\nexport function tunedRow(carId, install = {}) {\n  const d = { ...PHYS[carId] }, p = install.parts ?? {}, s = install.settings ?? {};\n  let power = 1;\n  if (p.exhaust) power *= 1.04;\n  if (p.intake) power *= 1.06;\n  if (p.engine) { power *= POWER_ENGINE[p.engine]; d.rpmPeak += RPM_PEAK[p.engine]; d.redline += RPM_RED[p.engine]; d.upshift += RPM_RED[p.engine]; }\n  if (p.turbo) {\n    if (d.turbo) power *= p.turbo === 1 ? 1.15 : 1.35;\n    else { power *= p.turbo === 1 ? 1.25 : 1.5; d.turbo = true; d.turboLag = 0.8; }\n  }\n  d.powerPS = Math.round(d.powerPS * power);\n  const cg0 = d.cgH ?? 0.5; let cg = cg0;\n  if (p.weight) { d.massKg = Math.round(d.massKg * [1, 0.95, 0.9, 0.85][p.weight]); cg *= [1, 0.99, 0.98, 0.96][p.weight]; }\n  if (p.clutch) d.shiftTime = 0.11;\n  if (p.gearbox) { d.shiftTime = 0.08; d.final = d.final * (s.gearing ?? 1); }\n  if (p.lsd) d.lsd = s.lsd ?? Math.max(d.lsd ?? 0, 0.5);\n  if (p.suspension === 1) { d.loadK = 0.085; cg *= 0.96; }\n  if (p.suspension === 2) { d.loadK = 0.07; cg *= 0.92; cg *= s.ride ?? 1; }\n  if (p.suspension) d.rollF = s.balance ?? d.rollF;\n  d.cgH = cg;\n  const brakeBase = d.brakeG ?? 1.25;\n  if (p.brakes === 1) d.brakeG = brakeBase + 0.15;\n  if (p.brakes === 2) { d.brakeG = brakeBase + 0.4; d.brakeF = s.brakeBias ?? 0.62; }\n  const clA = d.clA ?? 0.1, cdA = d.cdA ?? 0.7;\n  if (p.aero === 1) { d.clA = clA + 0.15; d.cdA = cdA + 0.02; }\n  if (p.aero === 2) { d.clA = clA + 0.5 * (s.downforce ?? 1); d.cdA = cdA + 0.06 * (s.downforce ?? 1); }\n  if (install.tyre) { const t = TYRE[install.tyre]; d.tyreMu = t.tyreMu; d.alphaP = t.alphaP; d.tyreTable = { dirt: t.dirt, gravel: t.dirt }; d.wearX = t.wearX; }\n  d.exhaustUp = !!p.exhaust;\n  d.jolty = (p.suspension === 2 && (s.ride ?? 1) < 0.94);\n  return d;\n}\nexport const tunedParams = (carId, install) => ({ ...carParams(tunedRow(carId, install)), carId });\n/** Shown power and weight: what event limits read. */\nexport function specOf(carId, install) { const d = tunedRow(carId, install); return { ps: d.powerPS, kg: d.massKg, layout: d.layout, tyre: install?.tyre ?? null }; }\n/** A dyno curve: PS across the rev range, for the before/after draw. */\nexport function dynoCurve(carId, install, torqueShape, points = 40) {\n  const d = tunedRow(carId, install), p = carParams(d), out = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < points; i++) { const rpm = 1500 + ((d.redline - 1500) * i) / (points - 1), x = rpm / d.rpmPeak, boost = d.turbo ? (rpm > d.rpmPeak * 0.4 ? 1 : 0.62) : 1, w = (rpm * 2 * Math.PI) / 60; out.push({ rpm, ps: (p.Tpeak * torqueShape(x, d) * boost * w) / 735.5 }); }\n  return { curve: out, peak: Math.max(...out.map((o) => o.ps)), redline: d.redline };\n}\nE\ncat > src/game/data/licences.js <<'E'\n// Licence tests as data. from/to resolve against a track (corner index c plus metres off, or a raw s from the start line).\nimport { MEDALS } from './medals.gen.js';\nconst t = (id, title, carId, track, o) => ({ id, title, carId, track, medals: MEDALS[id], ...o });\nexport const LICENCES = [\n  { id: 'C', name: 'PROVISIONAL', reward: 2000, goldLine: 'A PICO, AS A PRIZE. PLEASE LOOK AFTER IT.', goldCar: 'pico', blurb: 'THE FIRST CLIPBOARD. THE KITE, THE PROVING GROUND.', tests: ['C-1', 'C-2', 'C-3', 'C-4'] },\n  { id: 'B', name: 'CLUB', reward: 5000, goldLine: 'A CASTELLAN MOTH, AS A PRIZE. IT WAS IN THE WAY.', goldCar: 'moth', blurb: 'REAR-WHEEL DRIVE. KESTREL PARK.', tests: ['B-1', 'B-2', 'B-3', 'B-4'] },\n  { id: 'A', name: 'NATIONAL', reward: 10000, goldLine: '25,000 CREDITS AND A GOLD HELMET FOR THE SHELF.', goldCredits: 25000, goldHelmet: true, blurb: 'CEDAR, RED CLAY AND THE HARBOUR AT NIGHT.', tests: ['A-1', 'A-2', 'A-3', 'A-4'] },\n];\nexport const LICENCE = Object.fromEntries(LICENCES.map((l) => [l.id, l]));\nexport const TESTS = [\n  t('C-1', 'START AND STOP', 'kite', 'proving', { standing: true, from: { s: -300 }, box: { at: 100, len: 30 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'THE BRAKE IS A PEDAL WITH A FAR END.',\n    brief: 'Accelerate to the marker, then bring the car to rest inside the white box. Please remember: the brake is also a steering wheel.', tip: 'BRAKE EARLY. THE BOX WILL WAIT.' }),\n  t('C-2', 'FIRST CORNER', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 0, off: -100 }, to: { c: 1, off: 100 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'TURN IN, APEX, UNWIND.',\n    brief: 'One corner, driven properly. Turn in, touch the apex, and let the car run wide on the way out.', tip: 'SLOW IN, FAST OUT. THIS HAS BEEN TRUE FOR SOME TIME.' }),\n  t('C-3', 'CONE WEAVE', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 50, from: { s: -200 }, to: { s: 200 }, cones: { at: -120, n: 6, gap: 40 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'WEIGHT MOVES.',\n    brief: 'Pass the cones on alternate sides, starting on the left. Each cone hit or missed adds one second. The cones are not angry. They are only cones.', tip: 'STEER EARLY. THE CAR ARRIVES LATER THAN YOU DO.' }),\n  t('C-4', 'THE SHORT LOOP', 'kite', 'proving', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 2, off: -50 }, to: { c: 6, off: 50 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'LINK CORNERS. KEEP YOUR HEAD UP.',\n    brief: 'Five corners in a row. Each one begins where the last one ended. Please look ahead of the car.', tip: 'THE EXIT OF ONE CORNER IS THE ENTRY OF THE NEXT.' }),\n  t('B-1', 'THRESHOLD', 'ginga', 'proving', { startSpeed: 160, from: { s: -60 }, box: { at: 105, len: 30 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: { abs: false }, lesson: \"SQUEEZE, DON'T STAMP.\",\n    brief: 'The ABS is off for this test. Stop inside the box. Locking the wheels is allowed. It is not admired.', tip: 'A TYRE THAT IS LOCKED IS ONLY A SLED.' }),\n  t('B-2', 'HAIRPIN EXIT', 'ginga', 'kestrel', { startSpeed: 90, from: { c: 5, off: -150 }, to: { c: 7, off: 60 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: { tcs: 0 }, lesson: 'FEED THE THROTTLE.',\n    brief: 'Traction control is off. The rear tyres will do as they are told, if they are told slowly.', tip: 'OPEN THE THROTTLE AS YOU OPEN THE STEERING.' }),\n  t('B-3', 'THREE LAYOUTS', 'kite', 'proving', { runs: ['kite', 'ginga', 'ryu'], startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'FF, FR, 4WD IN THE SAME CORNERS.',\n    brief: 'The same four corners, in three cars. Front drive, rear drive, all four. The times are added. You will have a favourite. Please keep it to yourself.', tip: 'EACH CAR WANTS A DIFFERENT THROTTLE.' }),\n  t('B-4', 'ONE LAP OF KESTREL', 'ginga', 'kestrel', { flying: true, startSpeed: 110, from: { s: -220 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'RHYTHM.',\n    brief: 'One flying lap of Kestrel Park. The windmill is not part of the course. Many have asked.', tip: 'DO NOT HURRY. BE EARLY.' }),\n  t('A-1', 'BLIND CREST', 'brandt32', 'cedar', { startSpeed: 90, from: { c: 3, off: -100 }, to: { c: 5, off: 100 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'TRUST THE ROAD YOU REMEMBER.',\n    brief: 'The road goes over the crest and turns. You cannot see this. You must remember it.', tip: 'A CREST TAKES WEIGHT FROM ALL FOUR TYRES AT ONCE.' }),\n  t('A-2', 'SWITCHBACKS', 'moth', 'cedar', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'MOMENTUM.',\n    brief: 'The Moth has 135 PS and the road goes uphill. What you have when you arrive is what you keep.', tip: 'A SMOOTH LINE IS A CHEAP SOURCE OF POWER.' }),\n  t('A-3', 'RED CLAY', 'ryuRally', 'redclay', { startSpeed: 60, from: { c: 7 }, to: { c: 10 }, limits: { offroad: false }, assists: {}, lesson: 'ROTATE WITH THE HANDBRAKE.',\n    brief: 'Dirt. Use the handbrake to turn the car in the slow corners. It is not rude here.', tip: 'LOOK WHERE YOU WISH TO GO. THE CAR IS GOING SOMEWHERE ELSE.' }),\n  t('A-4', 'HARBOUR AT NIGHT', 'libeccio', 'harbour', { flying: true, startSpeed: 90, hour: 21, from: { s: -200 }, limits: { offroad: true }, assists: {}, lesson: 'EVERYTHING, BY LAMPLIGHT.',\n    brief: 'One flying lap of the Harbour. The walls are close and it is dark. There is no margin. I will be here.', tip: 'THE LAMPS MARK THE CORNERS. COUNT THEM.' }),\n];\nexport const TEST = Object.fromEntries(TESTS.map((x) => [x.id, x]));\nE\ncat > src/game/data/medals.gen.js <<'E'\nexport const MEDALS = {};\nE\ncat > src/game/data/events.js <<'E'\n// Events as data. Rounds: [track, laps, {hour, rain}]. pool entries: car id plus an optional tuned install.\nconst T1 = { parts: { exhaust: 1, intake: 1, engine: 1, suspension: 1, weight: 1 }, tyre: 'sport' };\nconst T2 = { parts: { exhaust: 1, intake: 1, engine: 2, suspension: 2, weight: 2, brakes: 1 }, tyre: 'semi' };\nconst r = (track, laps, o = {}) => ({ track, laps, ...o });\nexport const POINTS = [10, 8, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1], PRIZE_RATIO = [1, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2];\nexport const EVENTS = [\n  { id: 'dawn', name: 'DAWN PATROL CUP', needs: 'C', limit: { maxPS: 210 }, limitText: '210 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('kestrel', 2), r('harbour', 2, { hour: 18.5 }), r('kestrel', 3)], pace: [0.86, 0.9], pool: [['pico'], ['kite'], ['moth']], prize: 1500, bonus: 3000,\n    intro: 'A CUP FOR THOSE WHO RISE EARLY AND HAVE NOT YET SPENT MUCH.' },\n  { id: 'fellow', name: 'FRONT-DRIVE FELLOWSHIP', needs: 'C', limit: { maxPS: 230, layout: 'FF' }, limitText: 'FRONT DRIVE, 230 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 2), r('saltline', 4)], pace: [0.88, 0.91], pool: [['kite'], ['kite', T1], ['pico', T1]], prize: 2000, bonus: 5000,\n    intro: 'THE MEMBERS MEET ANNUALLY TO DISCUSS UNDERSTEER. THEY ARE IN FAVOUR.' },\n  { id: 'feather', name: 'FEATHERWEIGHT TROPHY', needs: 'B', limit: { maxKg: 1100 }, limitText: '1,100 KG OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 3), r('kestrel', 3), r('harbour', 3, { hour: 18.5 })], pace: [0.9, 0.93], pool: [['moth'], ['kiteCup'], ['pico', T1]], prize: 3000, bonus: 8000, prizeCar: 'kiteCup',\n    intro: 'THE SCALES ARE CHECKED EACH MORNING. THE DRIVERS HAVE STOPPED EATING LUNCH.' },\n  { id: 'society', name: 'REAR-DRIVE SOCIETY', needs: 'B', limit: { layout: 'FR' }, limitText: 'FRONT ENGINE, REAR DRIVE', rounds: [r('kestrel', 3, { rain: true }), r('saltline', 5)], pace: [0.91, 0.94], pool: [['ginga'], ['brandt32'], ['longhorn']], prize: 3500, bonus: 10000,\n    intro: 'A GENTLE SOCIETY. IT MEETS IN THE RAIN, ON PURPOSE.' },\n  { id: 'clay', name: 'RED CLAY RALLY', needs: 'B', limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR. DIRT TYRES ADVISED', rally: true, rounds: [r('redclay', 2), r('redclay', 2), r('redclay', 2)], pace: [0.91, 0.95], pool: [['ryu'], ['ryuRally']], prize: 4000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'ryuRally',\n    intro: 'THREE LEGS AGAINST ONE RIVAL EACH. WIN TWO. THE CLOCK DECIDES.' },\n  { id: 'touring', name: 'PENINSULA TOURING TROPHY', needs: 'A', limit: { maxPS: 520 }, limitText: '520 PS OR LESS', rounds: [r('cedar', 3), r('harbour', 3, { hour: 21 }), r('saltline', 6), r('kestrel', 4)], pace: [0.93, 0.96], pool: [['brandt32'], ['heck'], ['libeccio'], ['longhorn'], ['ryu', T1]], prize: 6000, bonus: 40000, prizeCar: 'corsa',\n    intro: 'FOUR ROUNDS, THE WHOLE PENINSULA. BRING A SANDWICH.' },\n  { id: 'h200', name: 'HARBOUR LIGHTS 200', needs: 'A', limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR. ONE PIT STOP NEEDED', endurance: true, rounds: [r('harbour', 10, { hour: 18.5, hourEnd: 21 })], pace: [0.92, 0.95], pool: [['heck'], ['libeccio'], ['brandt32', T2]], prize: 20000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'works', field: 8,\n    intro: 'TEN LAPS, DUSK INTO NIGHT. THE TYRES WILL NOT LAST. THE FUEL WILL NOT LAST. PLEASE STOP ONCE.' },\n  { id: 'gp', name: 'THE HALCYON GRAND PRIX', needs: 'A', needsEvent: ['touring', 'h200'], limit: {}, limitText: 'ANY CAR', rounds: [r('kestrel', 5), r('cedar', 5), r('saltline', 8), r('harbour', 5, { hour: 21 })], pace: [0.96, 0.99], pool: [['works'], ['corsa'], ['libeccio', T2]], prize: 30000, bonus: 0, prizeCar: 'type9', ending: true,\n    intro: 'THE LAST EVENT. THE PENINSULA WILL BE WATCHING, IN ITS QUIET WAY.' },\n];\nexport const EVENT = Object.fromEntries(EVENTS.map((e) => [e.id, e]));\nexport const DRIVERS = ['A. MORETTI', 'K. HANDA', 'J. OAKES', 'L. BRANDVOLD', 'S. AOKI', 'P. DELACROIX', 'T. WREN', 'R. OSEI', 'M. VANTER', 'D. IGARASHI', 'C. HOLLOWAY', 'E. RASK'];\nE\ncat > src/game/sim/career.js <<'E'\n// Pure rules of the career: money, licences, events, prizes, oil, days. No engine, no DOM.\nimport { CARS, CAR_LIST } from '../data/cars.js';\nimport { PART, PAINT_PRICE, RIM_PRICE, OIL_PRICE, WASH_PRICE, SETTINGS } from '../data/parts.js';\nimport { TYRE } from '../data/tyres.js';\nimport { LICENCES, LICENCE, TEST } from '../data/licences.js';\nimport { EVENT, EVENTS, POINTS, PRIZE_RATIO } from '../data/events.js';\nimport { STARTING_CREDITS, PROFILE_VERSION } from '../data/meta.js';\nimport { specOf, emptyInstall } from './tuning.js';\n\nexport function newProfile() {\n  return { v: PROFILE_VERSION, credits: STARTING_CREDITS, day: 1, cars: [], current: null, nextUid: 1, tests: {}, licences: {}, events: {}, seen: {}, trophies: [], assists: { abs: true, tcs: 5, asm: 5, auto: true, line: false }, records: {}, stats: { km: 0, wins: 0, races: 0, golds: 0, spent: 0, earned: 0 }, greeted: false, ended: false, replays: [], ghosts: {}, failStreak: {} };\n}\n/** Older saves move forward one version at a time. */\nexport function migrate(p) {\n  if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return newProfile();\n  if (!p.v || p.v < 2) { p.seen ??= {}; p.trophies ??= []; p.v = 2; }\n  if (p.v < 3) { p.replays ??= []; p.ghosts ??= {}; p.failStreak ??= {}; for (const c of p.cars ?? []) { c.dirt ??= 0; c.oilKm ??= 0; c.install ??= emptyInstall(); } p.v = 3; }\n  return p;\n}\nexport const carRec = (p, uid = p.current) => p.cars.find((c) => c.uid === uid) ?? null;\nexport const hasCar = (p, id) => p.cars.some((c) => c.id === id);\nfunction giveCar(p, id, bought) {\n  const rec = { uid: p.nextUid++, id, install: emptyInstall(), km: bought ? 40000 + (id.length * 7919) % 50000 : 0, oilKm: bought && CARS[id].where === 'used' ? 900 : 0, dirt: 0, wins: 0, prize: !bought };\n  if (CARS[id].where !== 'used') rec.km = bought ? 12 : 0;\n  rec.install.paint = CARS[id].paint;\n  p.cars.push(rec); p.seen[id] = true;\n  if (p.current == null) p.current = rec.uid;\n  return rec;\n}\nexport function canBuy(p, id) {\n  const c = CARS[id];\n  if (!c.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT FOR SALE' };\n  if (c.afterA && !p.licences.A) return { ok: false, why: 'LICENCE A REQUIRED' };\n  if (p.credits < c.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT ENOUGH CREDITS' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function buyCar(p, id) { const can = canBuy(p, id); if (!can.ok) return null; p.credits -= CARS[id].price; p.stats.spent += CARS[id].price; const rec = giveCar(p, id, true); p.current = rec.uid; return rec; }\nexport function canSell(p, uid) {\n  const r = carRec(p, uid);\n  if (!r) return { ok: false, why: 'NO SUCH CAR' };\n  if (p.cars.length <= 1) return { ok: false, why: 'YOUR LAST CAR. THEN WHAT?' };\n  if (r.prize) return { ok: false, why: 'PRIZE CARS ARE NOT FOR SALE. IT IS SIMPLY NOT DONE.' };\n  return { ok: true, value: Math.floor(CARS[r.id].price / 2) };\n}\nexport function sellCar(p, uid) { const can = canSell(p, uid); if (!can.ok) return 0; p.credits += can.value; p.cars = p.cars.filter((c) => c.uid !== uid); if (p.current === uid) p.current = p.cars[0].uid; return can.value; }\n\n// ---- parts\nexport function partOwned(rec, part) { const v = rec.install.parts[part.slot]; return part.level === v; }\nexport function partSuperseded(rec, part) { const v = rec.install.parts[part.slot]; return !!v && v > part.level; }\nexport function canBuyPart(p, rec, part) {\n  if (partOwned(rec, part)) return { ok: false, why: 'FITTED' };\n  if (p.credits < part.price) return { ok: false, why: 'NOT ENOUGH CREDITS' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function buyPart(p, rec, partId) {\n  const part = PART[partId], can = canBuyPart(p, rec, part);\n  if (!can.ok) return false;\n  p.credits -= part.price; p.stats.spent += part.price; rec.install.parts[part.slot] = part.level;\n  for (const s of SETTINGS) if (s.needs(rec.install.parts) && rec.install.settings[s.id] == null) rec.install.settings[s.id] = s.id === 'balance' ? CARS[rec.id].phys.rollF ?? s.def : s.def;\n  return true;\n}\nexport function buyTyre(p, rec, id) { const t = TYRE[id]; if (rec.install.tyre === id || p.credits < t.price) return false; p.credits -= t.price; p.stats.spent += t.price; rec.install.tyre = id; return true; }\nexport function buyPaint(p, rec, colour) { if (p.credits < PAINT_PRICE || rec.install.paint === colour) return false; p.credits -= PAINT_PRICE; p.stats.spent += PAINT_PRICE; rec.install.paint = colour; return true; }\nexport function buyRims(p, rec, id) { if (p.credits < RIM_PRICE || rec.install.rims === id) return false; p.credits -= RIM_PRICE; p.stats.spent += RIM_PRICE; rec.install.rims = id; return true; }\n\n// ---- service\nexport function oilFactor(rec) {\n  const km = rec?.oilKm ?? 0;\n  if (km < 100 && rec?.oilFresh) return 1.02;\n  if (km <= 200) return 1;\n  return Math.max(0.92, 1 - Math.floor((km - 200) / 40) * 0.005);\n}\nexport function changeOil(p, rec) { if (p.credits < OIL_PRICE) return false; p.credits -= OIL_PRICE; p.stats.spent += OIL_PRICE; rec.oilKm = 0; rec.oilFresh = true; return true; }\nexport function washCar(p, rec) { if (p.credits < WASH_PRICE) return false; p.credits -= WASH_PRICE; p.stats.spent += WASH_PRICE; rec.dirt = 0; return true; }\nexport function addMileage(p, rec, metres, dirtGain = 0) { const km = metres / 1000; p.stats.km += km; if (rec) { rec.km += km; rec.oilKm += km; rec.dirt = Math.min(1, rec.dirt + dirtGain); } }\n\n// ---- licences\nexport const licenceOrder = ['C', 'B', 'A'];\nexport const licenceHeld = (p, id) => !!p.licences[id];\nexport const licenceOpen = (p, id) => id === 'C' || licenceHeld(p, licenceOrder[licenceOrder.indexOf(id) - 1]);\nexport const medalName = (m) => [null, 'BRONZE', 'SILVER', 'GOLD'][m];\nexport function medalFor(test, time) { const m = test.medals; if (!m) return 0; return time <= m.gold ? 3 : time <= m.silver ? 2 : time <= m.bronze ? 1 : 0; }\n/** Record an attempt; returns what happened so the screens can say it. */\nexport function applyTest(p, testId, time, failed = false, dev = false) {\n  const test = TEST[testId], medal = failed ? 0 : medalFor(test, time), out = { medal, licenceWon: null, reward: 0, goldBonus: null, newBest: false };\n  if (medal === 0) { p.failStreak[testId] = (p.failStreak[testId] ?? 0) + 1; return out; }\n  p.failStreak[testId] = 0;\n  if (dev) return out;\n  const prev = p.tests[testId] ?? { medal: 0, time: Infinity };\n  if (medal === 3 && prev.medal < 3) p.stats.golds++;\n  if (medal > prev.medal || time < prev.time) out.newBest = true;\n  p.tests[testId] = { medal: Math.max(prev.medal, medal), time: Math.min(prev.time, time) };\n  const lic = LICENCE[testId[0]];\n  if (!p.licences[lic.id] && lic.tests.every((t) => p.tests[t]?.medal >= 1)) { p.licences[lic.id] = true; p.credits += lic.reward; p.stats.earned += lic.reward; out.licenceWon = lic.id; out.reward = lic.reward; }\n  if (p.licences[lic.id] && !p.goldDone?.[lic.id] && lic.tests.every((t) => p.tests[t]?.medal === 3)) {\n    (p.goldDone ??= {})[lic.id] = true; out.goldBonus = lic.id;\n    if (lic.goldCar && !hasCar(p, lic.goldCar)) giveCar(p, lic.goldCar, false);\n    if (lic.goldCredits) { p.credits += lic.goldCredits; p.stats.earned += lic.goldCredits; }\n    if (lic.goldHelmet) p.trophies.push({ kind: 'helmet', name: `GOLD HELMET`, day: p.day });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n// ---- events\nexport function eventOpen(p, id) {\n  const e = EVENT[id];\n  if (!p.licences[e.needs]) return { ok: false, why: `LICENCE ${e.needs} REQUIRED` };\n  if (e.needsEvent && !e.needsEvent.some((x) => p.events[x]?.won)) return { ok: false, why: 'WIN THE TOURING TROPHY OR THE HARBOUR 200' };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport function carQualifies(e, carId, install) {\n  const s = specOf(carId, install), l = e.limit;\n  if (l.maxPS && s.ps > l.maxPS) return { ok: false, why: `${s.ps} PS. THE LIMIT IS ${l.maxPS}.` };\n  if (l.maxKg && s.kg > l.maxKg) return { ok: false, why: `${s.kg} KG. THE LIMIT IS ${l.maxKg}.` };\n  if (l.layout && s.layout !== l.layout) return { ok: false, why: `THIS EVENT IS FOR ${l.layout} CARS ONLY.` };\n  return { ok: true };\n}\nexport const eventState = (p, id) => (p.events[id] ??= { round: 0, points: {}, won: false, wins: 0, best: null });\n/** results: [{ key, name, player }] in finishing order. Returns the money and the state of the series. */\nexport function applyRound(p, eventId, results, prizeScale = 1) {\n  const e = EVENT[eventId], st = eventState(p, eventId), out = { place: 0, money: 0, points: 0, seriesOver: false, seriesWon: false, bonus: 0, prizeCar: null, standings: [], ending: false };\n  results.forEach((r, i) => { const pts = POINTS[i] ?? 0; st.points[r.key] = (st.points[r.key] ?? 0) + pts; if (r.player) { out.place = i + 1; out.points = pts; } });\n  out.money = Math.round(((PRIZE_RATIO[out.place - 1] ?? 0) * e.prize * prizeScale) / 10) * 10;\n  p.credits += out.money; p.stats.earned += out.money; p.stats.races++; p.day++;\n  if (out.place === 1) p.stats.wins++;\n  st.round++;\n  out.standings = Object.entries(st.points).sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1]);\n  if (st.round >= e.rounds.length) {\n    out.seriesOver = true;\n    const my = st.points.player ?? 0, top = Math.max(...Object.entries(st.points).filter(([k]) => k !== 'player').map(([, v]) => v), 0);\n    out.seriesWon = my > top;\n    if (out.seriesWon) {\n      const first = !st.won;\n      st.won = true; st.wins = (st.wins ?? 0) + 1; out.bonus = Math.round(e.bonus * prizeScale); p.credits += out.bonus; p.stats.earned += out.bonus;\n      if (e.prizeCar && first && !hasCar(p, e.prizeCar)) { giveCar(p, e.prizeCar, false); out.prizeCar = e.prizeCar; }\n      p.trophies.push({ kind: 'cup', name: e.name, day: p.day });\n      if (e.ending && first) { out.ending = true; p.ended = true; }\n    }\n    st.round = 0; st.points = {};\n  }\n  return out;\n}\nexport function resetEvent(p, id) { const st = eventState(p, id); st.round = 0; st.points = {}; }\n\nexport function record(p, trackId, lap, carName) { const r = p.records[trackId]; if (!r || lap < r.lap) { p.records[trackId] = { lap, car: carName }; return true; } return false; }\n/** Share of the world collected, for the Garage. */\nexport function collected(p) {\n  const cars = new Set(p.cars.map((c) => c.id)).size, tests = Object.keys(p.tests).length, ev = EVENTS.filter((e) => p.events[e.id]?.won).length;\n  return Math.round(((cars + tests + ev) / (CAR_LIST.length + 12 + EVENTS.length)) * 100);\n}\n/** One line saying what to try next on the Map. */\nexport function nudge(p) {\n  if (!p.cars.length) return { place: 'dealer', text: 'FIRST, A CAR. DEALER ROW HAS THREE YOU CAN AFFORD.' };\n  if (!p.licences.C) return { place: 'licence', text: 'NOW, A LICENCE. MS. ARAI IS WAITING AT THE TOWER.' };\n  if (!EVENT.dawn || !p.events.dawn?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE DAWN PATROL CUP WILL ACCEPT YOU. THE EVENT HALL IS OPEN.' };\n  const r = carRec(p);\n  if (r && r.oilKm > 300) return { place: 'service', text: 'YOUR OIL IS TIRED. BENNO HAS MENTIONED IT.' };\n  if (!Object.keys(r?.install.parts ?? {}).length) return { place: 'tuning', text: 'YOU HAVE MONEY. BRAKE PADS ARE A GOOD FIRST THOUGHT.' };\n  if (!p.licences.B) return { place: 'licence', text: 'THE CLUB LICENCE IS NEXT. PLEASE BRING A REAR-DRIVE ATTITUDE.' };\n  if (!p.events.feather?.won && !p.events.society?.won && !p.events.clay?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THREE NEW EVENTS AWAIT THE CLUB LICENCE.' };\n  if (!p.licences.A) return { place: 'licence', text: 'THE NATIONAL LICENCE. MS. ARAI HAS CLEARED HER AFTERNOON.' };\n  if (!p.events.touring?.won && !p.events.h200?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE TOURING TROPHY AND THE HARBOUR 200 ARE OPEN TO YOU.' };\n  if (!p.events.gp?.won) return { place: 'events', text: 'THE GRAND PRIX. THE LIGHTS ARE ON FOR YOU NOW.' };\n  return { place: 'home', text: 'YOU MAY KEEP DRIVING. MOST PEOPLE DO.' };\n}\nexport { LICENCES, EVENTS };\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\nprint(\"ok\")\nE\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'E'\n- Sim extracted from plan and passes lap regression (tools/tests/reg0.mjs -> move into sim suite). data/* and sim/career, tuning written.\nE\nls ..","description":"Write data modules, tuning and career rules"}}}
