{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkvoXFtJdNgAejxCugC4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now gone through the plan's \"Before you stop\" list, and everything that can be done on this computer is done. All eight suites pass on the final build (852 checks). The full 1080p review found one more real bug, now fixed.\n\n## Before-you-stop checklist\n\n| Plan item | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `node tools/test.mjs` all green, hub passing all three runs | ✅ 852 passed, 0 failed, run from scratch on this build |\n| Scripted playthrough finishes the career with no Dev tools | ✅ passes, including a check that dev tools stayed off |\n| HTML runs from `file://`, `session.js` unmodified and first, engine unedited | ✅ browser suite runs from `file://`; the client text is in the HTML byte for byte, ahead of everything but the charset tag; the engine matched the released kit when I compared them, and I haven't touched it since |\n| Music at 10% on a fresh profile and in a session | ✅ both are tested, the session in all three hub runs |\n| Grep for TODO, FIXME, placeholder, stub, coming soon | ✅ 0 hits across the game code, docs and hub tags |\n| Every menu item works; every car, track, test and event reachable | ✅ data, headless, browser and play suites; attract clips, Couch Duel and every top-level screen were also driven directly |\n| Looked at the 1080p screenshots | ✅ the plan's full list, see below |\n| About/Credits shows real answers; exit interview parses; chat matches | ✅ the exit interview parses and every feedback answer is in the built game; the About fields are checked by the browser suite |\n| No stray servers or browsers of mine | ✅ none running; scratch files removed |\n\n## The 1080p review\nI viewed these with no console errors:\n- all 14 cars in the showroom\n- all six tracks at the start and at a corner\n- the Map by day, at dusk and at night\n- the race HUD, results, replay, Settings, Handbook, Tuning and the other menu screens\n- Harbour at night and Couch Duel\n- the rally crest in the air and on landing, where the landing dust is visible\n- the pit stop, podium, prize reveal and ending\n- all ten attract clips\n\n**The bug it found:** on Saltline, the ground beside the banked road ignored the bank and stood about 2 m above the road edge, which hid the lower half of the car. The pit building and stands were at the wrong height too. I fixed the geometry and added a longer leg on the start gantry's low side. This is issue 31 in the list in `PROGRESS.md`, and the exit interview now says 31.\n\n**Re-shot after that fix:** Saltline, Cedar and the Saltline attract clip. The fix only moves ground and buildings on banked roads, and only those two tracks have banks, so I didn't re-shoot the others.\n\n## What can't be done here\nThe plan says real hardware is \"checked as far as it can be here, never required\", so these rest on stand-ins:\n- **Controller:** tested with a stubbed pad, so analog feel on a real DualSense is unproven.\n- **TV and sound:** judged from screenshots and by measuring the audio, not by watching or listening.\n- **Balance:** tuned against a bot at 0.97 skill. No human has played it, so handling feel and difficulty are the first things to try.\n- **WebKit and real iOS:** not run; WebKit has no WebGPU on this machine.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback answers from my earlier reply still stand, apart from the issue count, now 31 with 12 seen only in screenshots. The critical count stays at 5.\n\nEverything is in `work/`:\n- `GrandpaTurismo-GranTurismo3ASpec-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171907.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `GrandpaTurismo-GranTurismo3ASpec-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171907/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":681740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":321},"output_tokens":708,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c060cbf0-9de2-4b69-aed6-69ef0ff7f0ee","uuid":"d16b7e82-fbc9-480f-8657-745383b1c92b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:01:11.410Z","request_id":"req_011CgkvoWsJwzCkpNTW4dMtm"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript shows the final build's suites passing (852 checks), the playthrough passing, and the deliverables present in the work folder. But the completion condition is not clearly met. The last full 1080p review was run before the Saltline bank fix, and the fix was followed only by re-shooting Saltline, Cedar and the attract clip, not every track and menu. The plan's 'Before you stop' list also asks that the 1080p check be done after the final changes. The transcript also shows the agent's own summary claiming 'The Source Information and feedback answers... still stand' while the exit interview's issue count was changed by editing rather than verified against a list. The plan's requirement that every item be done on this computer and verified in the transcript has therefore not been clearly demonstrated."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c060cbf0-9de2-4b69-aed6-69ef0ff7f0ee","uuid":"8997b25c-791e-4fdc-b43c-8a6687486149","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:01:24.765Z","isSynthetic":true}
