{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkwMCsyApk98fpfpWAJb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook's remaining points are closed: I reviewed the full 1080p list on the exact final build, and all 852 test checks pass on that same build. No code changed during this pass; the HTML's hash (`8197d35509c2`) was the same before and after the screenshots.\n\n## The hook's two points\n- **1080p review after the final change:** I re-shot and looked at the whole list on that build, with no console errors:\n  - **Cars and tracks:** all 14 cars, and all six tracks at the start and at a corner.\n  - **Rally crest:** in the air (0.8 m up) and on landing, with the thump counted and dust visible.\n  - **Menus:** Title, the Map by day, at dusk and at night, Licence Centre, test card, Event Hall, event card, Tuning, Setup, Service Bay, Garage, Museum, Theatre, Arcade, Settings, Handbook and About.\n  - **Racing:** race HUD, results, replay, Couch Duel, Harbour at night and the pit stop.\n  - **Set pieces:** all ten attract clips, podium, prize reveal and ending.\n- **Issue count:** `PROGRESS.md` now has the numbered list, and a script confirmed items 1 to 31 are all there with none missing. That the count matches the list is checked; the list itself is still my own record of this session, not the output of a tracking tool.\n\n## Minor things I left alone\n- The Map at dusk and at full night look close to each other. It's still clearly later than the daytime Map, and the lit marquee shows, but the change is subtle.\n- The times on the results shot look odd only because my script used the dev \"finish now\" tool; a raced result shows real times.\n- The review shots use a test save, which is why Licence Centre reads \"0/4 passed, held\".\n\n## What still can't be done here\nReal pad, TV, speakers, a human driver and iOS Safari aren't available on this machine, and the plan says those are never required. Handling feel and difficulty are therefore unproven, and are the first things to try. Balance was tuned against a bot at 0.97 skill, and WebKit can't run the game here because it has no WebGPU.\n\nI also kept `tools/review.py` as a permanent script for re-shooting this list. The Source Information and feedback answers from my earlier reply stand, with the issue count at 31 (12 seen only in screenshots, 5 critical).\n\nEverything is in `work/`:\n- `GrandpaTurismo-GranTurismo3ASpec-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171907.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `GrandpaTurismo-GranTurismo3ASpec-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-171907/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":701855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776},"output_tokens":700,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c060cbf0-9de2-4b69-aed6-69ef0ff7f0ee","uuid":"cde2dd75-6883-46b8-b0c3-2d74e6c92728","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:08:17.907Z","request_id":"req_011CgkwMCVQv7sBLisFrYfuc"}
